    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0562" n="482" xml:id="pg482"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-01-18"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 18, 1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 748.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 736, of
                    October 1 last, I have the honor to inform you that I lost no time upon its
                    receipt in requesting the foreign office to furnish me with such facts as they
                    might be able to obtain relative to the case of Mr. Patrick Lennon, in order
                    that I might communicate them to you.</p>
                <p>I have just received a note from Lord Lansdowne in reply, inclosing a copy, which
                    I transmit herewith, of the oath taken by Mr. Lennon on December 1, 1899, as a
                    burgher of the South African Republic, which has been forwarded by the general
                    officer commanding in chief in South Africa.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d479-a1.xml" xpointer="d479-a1"/>
            </div>
